231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Manually tracking daily foreign exchange fluctuations or using bulky, bloated software tools is impractical for quick, on-the-fly calculations. Furthermore, standard programming assignments often rely on hardcoded static exchange rates, making them obsolete immediately upon market changes. There is a need for a streamlined, lightweight utility tool that can interact with live web services securely, parse responses without external software dependencies, and render exact localized financial symbols dynamically.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
